      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787399950993,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "We will use max heap here\n1. but the question is\nhow to get top 2 max elements\n\n2. first convert the array into \nthe fucking maxheap\n\n3. now how to get top 2 max\nelements ,if we do .peak() , we will got \nmax element\n\n4. if we pop two element , and do differnece\nand back it into the heap \n\n5. the question is how to stop \n; i think we stop when we don't have first element \nor second element",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "We will use max heap here\n1. but the question is\nhow to get top 2 max elements\n\n2. first convert the array into \nthe fucking maxheap\n\n3. now how to get top 2 max\nelements ,if we do .peak() , we will got \nmax element\n\n4. if we pop two element , and do differnece\nand back it into the heap \n\n5. the question is how to stop \n; i think we stop when we don't have first element \nor second element",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
